<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahmad Shah Abdali</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ahmad Shah Durrani</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahmad Shah Abdali, also known as Ahmad Shah <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durrani-empire">Durrani</a>, was an Afghan commander in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a>'s army who founded the Durrani Empire after Nader's death in 1747. He invaded northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> several times and defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-battle-of-panipat">Third Battle of Panipat</a> in 1761. His campaigns weakened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a> and influenced the rise of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> power in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ahmad-shah-abdali.jpg" alt="Ahmad Shah Abdali" width="311" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Ahmad-Shah_Durrani._Mughal_miniature._ca._1757,_Biblioth%C3%A8que_nationale_de_France_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
